<%= @title %>

An installation access token for your GitHub App "<%= @app_name %>" was submitted to GitHub's credential revocation API: <%= "#{GitHub.help_url}/rest/credentials/revoke#revoke-a-list-of-credentials" %>

To prevent unauthorized access, we have revoked this token to ensure that it can no longer be used to authenticate to GitHub: <%= "#{GitHub.help_url}/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/token-expiration-and-revocation" %>

To encourage reports and ensure that exposed tokens can be quickly and easily revoked, we do not require authentication for submissions. As a result, GitHub is unable to provide further information about the source of the reported token.

If you did not submit this token to GitHub's credential revocation API and you believe that your token was exposed, review any unauthorized applications and remove any you don't recognize: <%= "#{GitHub.help_url}/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/reviewing-your-authorized-integrations#reviewing-your-authorized-github-apps" %>
Review your security log to ensure that no malicious activity has occurred: <%= "#{GitHub.help_url}/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/reviewing-your-security-log" %>

To restore access, you may need to generate a new installation token: <%= "#{GitHub.help_url}/apps/creating-github-apps/authenticating-with-a-github-app/authenticating-as-a-github-app-installation" %>
You can view your GitHub Apps in your developer settings: <%= @developer_apps_url %>
